During a recent incident, we found that benchmarking optimizations on a single, small dataset led to misleading performance claims. Random noise in runs on small datasets caused large variations in results. Switch to a larger, more representative dataset. Additionally, ensure you cache intermediate results to avoid redundant computations, which can skew your benchmarking results.

To improve, we implemented a 5-run average with bootstrapped confidence intervals, using the entire parsed dataset. This gave us more stable and reliable metrics, helping us make informed decisions about optimizations. Precomputing and caching parts of the parsing pipeline also significantly reduced runtime variance. Always account for infrastructure limitations and consider using managed services to avoid overloading resources during benchmarks.

