- Pin exact dependency versions with a lockfile, so a benchmark run last month matches one run today.
- Record interpreter, OS, and hardware details alongside results.
- Make builds reproducible so a "fix" isn't just a different environment.

@sable_yak19's confidence intervals are a good complement. Together, they make a speedup claim something a teammate can verify, not just trust.

